<hr />
<p><strong>Buying BUBS Swedish Candy from Meh</strong></p>
<p>PROS:</p>
<ul>
<li>Pretty cheap.</li>
<li>Good variety: banana toffee, raspberry foam skulls, and fruity sour skulls.</li>
<li>Pretty good reviews on Amazon.</li>
</ul>
<p>CONS:</p>
<ul>
<li>No songs.</li>
<li>No adventures.</li>
<li>While it’s cheap, it still costs money.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p><strong>Finding a ticket to Mister Magenta’s Magical Confectionery so you can try his Gum-diddly-Globs, a candy of legend that has never been released to the public</strong></p>
<p>PROS:</p>
<ul>
<li>All the candy you can eat along the tour for no money.</li>
<li>In fact, you might <em>make</em> some money… if you steal the patent to the Gum-diddly-Globs for the strange businessman who approached you on the street.</li>
<li>Lots of songs sung by Mister Magenta’s pink-skinned, blue-haired employees, which is neat.</li>
</ul>
<p>CONS:</p>
<ul>
<li>The tour’s kind of going on a while.</li>
<li>This is a pretty big one: It does seem like a lot of your greedy tour-mates keep getting murdered and/or tortured for doing bad things? And that’s what the songs are about?</li>
<li>Which makes you worry about the whole patent-stealing scheme.</li>
<li>Man, that psychedelic tunnel was rough, especially with the whole fear-of-getting-murdered thing.</li>
<li>The Gum-diddly-Globs have a bit of a gasoline-y taste? And when you told that to Mister Magenta, he just nodded enthusiastically and said, “Exactly!” (The recipe is from a long time ago and maybe contains meat)</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p>CONCLUSION: Just get the gummy candy on Meh. It’s way less of a headache.</p>